# --- build output ---
bin/
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.a
*.lib
*.obj
*.exp
*.pdb
*.ilk

# --- generated test data (rebuild: go run ./gpu/vectors -n 512 -out gpu/vectors.bin) ---
gpu/vectors.bin

# --- local config: holds your wallet address ---
derostorm.json

# --- release archives ---
*.rar
*.zip
*.7z
*.tar.gz

# --- logs and profiler dumps ---
*.log
*.ncu-rep
*.nsys-rep

# --- local scratch, not part of the project ---
_local/

# --- one-off measurement binaries ---
# The native and CUDA experiment builds land beside their sources with a suffix
# saying which variant they are (sabench_s160, saprof_b1b, desc_test256). The
# *.exe rule above already covers them; this comment is here so the next person
# knows they are disposable and can be deleted at any time.

# --- measurement notes, kept local ---
# One directory per research wave: what was tried, what was measured, and what
# was reverted. Deliberately not committed -- these are working notes against
# one machine's numbers, and the conclusions that survived them are written up
# in the README instead. Drop this line to start tracking them.
research/

# --- analysis tool output ---
# graphify writes a call-graph cache here. It is tens of megabytes of derived
# JSON keyed by content hash, so it rebuilds from the tree on demand and must
# never be committed.
graphify-out/

# --- editor / OS ---
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
